id: pmc-4w23
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.7.28 and harmonize the production audit script
description: "pm-changelog was the last fleet package still declaring pm-cli 2026.7.27. Bump all version sites and harmonize audit:prod onto the cross-platform fleet form."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: deps,release
created_at: "2026-07-28T05:28:01.951Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T05:35:12.975Z"
deadline: "2026-07-29T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T05:29:22.746Z"
author: maintainer
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "All version sites report 2026.7.28, the installed CLI resolves to 2026.7.28, audit:prod matches the fleet cross-platform form, and release:check passes end to end."
resolution: fixed
expected_result: pm-changelog declares and resolves pm-cli 2026.7.28 and its audit gate is robust to ambient npm config on both POSIX and Windows.
actual_result: "All four version sites report 2026.7.28, the installed CLI resolves to 2026.7.28, audit:prod matches the fleet cross-platform form, and release:check passes end to end."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
  pmc-r0nj,related,"2026-07-28T05:28:01.951Z",maintainer,null
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T05:28:01.951Z",maintainer,Last package in the 2026.7.28 adoption wave
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T05:28:01.951Z",maintainer,"audit:prod must spawn npm through a shell on win32 because Node refuses to exec .cmd via spawn"
  "2026-07-28T05:35:12.974Z",maintainer,"Correction: the description and close reason both say 'all four version sites', but there are FIVE declarations changed in this package:\n\n1. package.json top-level version\n2. package.json peerDependencies '@unbrained/pm-cli' >=2026.7.28\n3. package.json devDependencies '@unbrained/pm-cli' ^2026.7.28\n4. manifest.json version\n5. the extension module version constant in src/extension.ts\n\nThe 'four' figure was carried over from packages where the peer and dev ranges are not both present. Flagged by CodeRabbit on PR #104.\n\nRecording this as a note rather than editing the close reason, consistent with how the other corrections in this wave were handled: item history is append-only and audited, so the record should show the correction rather than hide it."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T05:28:01.951Z",maintainer,"A bare npm audit --omit=dev aborts with EALLOWSCRIPTS when npm_config_allow_scripts is set,so the audit gate can fail for reasons unrelated to vulnerabilities"
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,version and audit script
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "npm run release:check",project,600
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  CHANGELOG.md,project,regenerated after close
close_reason: "Bumped to pm-cli 2026.7.28 across all four version sites and harmonized audit:prod onto the cross-platform fleet form verified on Windows CI; release:check passes end to end."
body: "Bumps package.json version, peerDependencies to >=2026.7.28, devDependencies to ^2026.7.28, manifest.json, and the extension module version constant in src/extension.ts. Replaces the bare npm audit invocation with the fleet Node helper."
